        <exercise id="_3153a984-698b-4cfd-aa54-9e96713c8c68" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00021">
            <para id="para-00107">A backyard farmer wants to enclose a rectangular space for a new garden within her fenced backyard. She has purchased 80 feet of wire fencing to enclose three sides, and she will use a section of the backyard fence as the fourth side. The function is graphed below. What is the maximum area, in square feet, that can be fenced in?</para>
            <para id="para-00108">Enter the maximum area in square feet.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00021">
            <para id="para-00109">Correct! The maximum area is 800 square feet.</para>
            <para id="para-00110">Try again. Revisit activity 9.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00111">The correct answer is 800. The maximum area is 800 square feet.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
